# CodeMirror 5 status (checked 2026-07): 5.65.21 is the latest 5.x. The line is
# in LEGACY maintenance — the GitHub mirror (codemirror/codemirror5) was
# archived 2026-04-16 and development moved upstream to code.haverbeke.berlin;
# the project itself calls CM5 "legacy". The CM5 choice is deliberate (single
# file, no build step, CSP-friendly); expect patches to be rare, not "none".
# The three CodeMirror filenames all end in .min for consistency with the other
# bundles, but only the core is actually minified. The `source` row of each is
# the path the vendored BYTES came from, which is what step 1 above re-downloads
# — for the stylesheet and the SQL mode that is the plain upstream file, and
# pointing those rows at a .min URL would make the next re-verification report a
# mismatch against a file nobody changed.
#
# The core is minified by jsDelivr ON DEMAND ("Do NOT use SRI with dynamically
# generated files", says its own banner), so even its consistent row can fail
# step 2 after a re-minification with no version change. Compare against the
# original lib/codemirror.js if that happens, rather than assuming tampering.
[codemirror/codemirror.min.js]
component = CodeMirror 5 (editor core; jsDelivr-minified lib/codemirror.js)
version   = 5.65.21
license   = MIT
source    = https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/codemirror@5.65.21/lib/codemirror.min.js
sha256    = 6b1388af5a30e6dad949ed0264a43487f5e7a6126c107e8f127798cbf0d02b9c

